==Game Jam Updates==
Back in September we unveiled our talented J-Mods’ latest Game Jam projects! You can read all about them [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/game-jam-v---summer-summit-2024?oldschool=1 here]. After an overwhelmingly positive poll, we're delighted to announce that Mini Menu Improvements and the Bank Deposit Refresh are now officially part of the game!

These changes are all about streamlining your gameplay and making life in Gielinor that little bit easier.

===Mini Menu Improvements===
Hold onto your capes, folks – it's time to say “Hello!” to the shiny new Mini Menu teleport options!

We’ve all been there – you’re having trouble in a boss fight, it’s time to gracefully bow out, but you’re too busy dealing with a giant teleport menu! Annoying, right? Well, not any more!

Now, you can simply hover over your minimenu to see all your teleport options in a neat little submenu. With a couple of clicks you can travel anywhere you please! If you prefer the classic feel, you can always select the old ‘rub’ or ‘teleport’ options to access the traditional menu.

[[File:Bank QoL & Mini Menu Improvements (1).gif|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-01-22/MiniMenu.gif here]!'']]

We’re pretty sure you’ll love the new system, but we want to hear from YOU! Share your thoughts on the [http://discord.gg/OSRS Old School RuneScape Discord], [https://www.reddit.com/r/2007scape/comments/1i78fd6/bank_qol_mini_menu_improvements/ Reddit], or [https://x.com/OldSchoolRS X] – we’re watching and waiting to hear how it feels in action.

===Bank QoL===
Once you’ve teleported to the Bank, you’ll be glad to see that we have another update which makes restocking your gear a breeze!

In both the Bank screen and the Deposit Box menu, you can now lock individual slots.

[[File:Bank QoL & Mini Menu Improvements (2).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-01-22/bank_locks.jpg here]!'']]

Locking a slot means that when you hit the Deposit-All button, your locked items won’t be accidentally banked. Never again will you arrive at your Slayer Task to find that those all-important supplies are sat twiddling their thumbs next to your massive stacks of loot.

Remember, the menu locks the SLOT, not the ITEM. If you’ve rearranged your Inventory after locking your slots, you can right-click to ‘Unlock’ them again. They’re off by default and take the place of the usual ‘Examine’ option. Visit the new Deposit Lock Settings menu to toggle them on.

This is opened from the Bank's settings menu:

[[File:Bank QoL & Mini Menu Improvements (3).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-01-22/BankSettingsMenu.jpg here]!'']]

We’ve also revamped the Deposit Box layout to align with your inventory, making it easier and more intuitive to locate your items at a glance.

[[File:Bank QoL & Mini Menu Improvements (4).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-01-22/bank_deposit_box.jpg here]!'']]

Additionally, if you’re tired of the deposit box asking how many items to deposit whenever you use items on it, you can now enable a setting to skip the item quantity check and always deposit everything in one go.

Lastly, we’ve moved the ‘Deposit Worn Items’ button further away to prevent misclicks.

We hope this delivers a smoother, hassle-free banking experience! Give it a try and share your thoughts - we’d love to hear from you!

