===Leagues V Reward Feedback===
We’ve been listening to your feedback on a few quirks with the Leagues reward kits, so let’s dive into some of the details and clear up any confusion!

===Building Rugs and Curtains===
So, you’ve been trying to place those fancy rugs and curtains from the Leagues kit, but something’s a bit... off? While other rewards (like the Nexus portal) let you just ‘Use’ the kit on your furniture, the rugs and curtains require a little more work.

So here’s the deal:

To place your new decor, you’ll need to right-click an empty hotspot, select ‘Build’, and pop into the Build menu. This system is consistent with how things worked for items of the same kind (think: Deadman Rug), but we're sorry if this threw you for a loop!

[[File:Bank QoL & Mini Menu Improvements (7).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-01-22/Rug%20(1).jpg here]!'']]

We’d love to hear whether this system works for you or if you’d prefer a different approach in future.

===Reward kits Affecting Multiple vs. Single Items===
Another head-scratcher has been how some rewards, like the Leagues V Spirit Tree Scroll, only affect one piece of furniture, while rewards in past Leagues let you slap the kit on'' ''everything of that type in your PoH.

So why the change?

Well, we wanted to give you more flexibility with your customization. When League VI rolls around we don’t want you to be stuck choosing just one style for your entire PoH. Imagine mixing and matching your Leagues V and League VI Portal Kits to create the perfect setup – now that’s what we call customisation!

We know it’s a shift, but we believe this will give you way more control over your PoH designs in the long run. As always, we appreciate your feedback and patience as we continue to refine and improve these systems. Keep those ideas coming – we’re listening!

And with that, another Leagues adventure wraps up... until next time!

